.TH ENGINECONFIG 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
EngineConfig \- Everything the engine needs to know about your game, passed once to engine_init()
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqengine.h\(dq
.ft B
typedef struct EngineConfig {
  const char *title;
  int   logical_w, logical_h;  /* the resolution your game code thinks in (0 -> 640x360) */
  int   window_scale;          /* initial window = logical * scale (0 -> 2) */
  int   tick_rate;             /* fixed updates per second (0 -> 60) */
  void *user;                  /* your game's state; the engine stores it, never reads it */
\&
  const char *org, *app;       /* per-user save directory via SDL_GetPrefPath; NULL -> cwd */
  bool   audio;                /* open an audio device */
  bool   text;                 /* init SDL_ttf (only if built with ENGINE_WITH_TTF) */
  bool   gamepad;              /* open gamepads as they appear */
  Scene *pause_scene;          /* pushed automatically when the window loses focus (NULL = don't) */
  Color  clear_color;          /* zero alpha -> dark blue-grey */
} EngineConfig;
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Everything the engine needs to know about your game, passed once to engine_init(). Zero fields take defaults, so a designated initializer naming only what you care about is the normal way to build one: (EngineConfig){ .title = "Cats", .user = &state, .audio = true }. The struct is read once during engine_init and never again; it may live on the stack of main().
.SH FIELDS
.TP
.B title
window title; NULL \-> "Game"
.TP
.B logical_w
width in logical pixels, the resolution your game code thinks in; 0 \-> 640. The window is scaled to fit and letterboxed, so drawing never has to know the real window size.
.TP
.B logical_h
height in logical pixels; 0 \-> 360
.TP
.B window_scale
initial window size = logical size x this; 0 \-> 2. The window stays resizable and F11 toggles fullscreen.
.TP
.B tick_rate
fixed simulation updates per second; 0 \-> 60. Scene.update receives dt = 1/tick_rate every call regardless of the display's refresh rate.
.TP
.B user
pointer to your game state (normally a static GameState in main.c). The engine stores it in Engine.user and never reads it; scenes cast it back with GameState *g = e\->user.
.TP
.B org
organization name for the per\-user save folder (SDL_GetPrefPath); with app, e.g. "mystudio". NULL \-> saves are written to the current working directory.
.TP
.B app
application name for the per\-user save folder; see org
.TP
.B audio
open the default audio device so audio_load/audio_play/audio_music work. If no device exists the engine logs it and Engine.has_audio stays false; audio calls then do nothing.
.TP
.B text
initialize SDL_ttf so text_load_font can open .ttf files. Only effective when the engine was built with ENGINE_WITH_TTF; otherwise fonts fall back to the built\-in 8x8 font.
.TP
.B gamepad
open the first gamepad that appears (and any that replaces it). Input.pad_* fields stay zero without it.
.TP
.B pause_scene
a scene the engine pushes by itself when the window loses focus (alt\-tab, clicking another window); NULL \-> nothing happens. Normally your pause overlay.
.TP
.B clear_color
the color the frame is cleared to before any scene renders; an alpha of 0 (the zero value) \-> dark blue\-grey { 20, 20, 30 }
.SH MODULE
core (src/engine/core/engine.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR engine_init (3),
.BR Engine (3),
.BR gge\-engine (7),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
